mcp/node_modules/@mcpfn/testing/README.md:25:Official conformance validates protocol behavior. McpFn scenarios validate product behavior. Production MCP servers should run both. For a protected local endpoint, use `runAuthenticatedOfficialConformance({ url, credential })`; it requires a literal loopback upstream, binds a temporary loopback-only streaming proxy, pins every request to the configured upstream path, injects bounded credential headers without printing them, and closes the proxy and attempts credential revocation/disposal after the pinned official runner exits. Credential cleanup retries up to three times. If all attempts fail, it throws `McpFnConformanceCleanupError`; retain that error and call `await error.retryCleanup()` after the provider recovers. The error contains no raw credential fields, and a successful retry releases the retained lease.
